ng 'svm' requires tuning the support vector machine's boundary via 'svm.cost' (4.5399929762484854e-05 to 22026.465794806718 with log-scale), 'svm.kernel' ('linear', 'polynomial', 'radial'), 'svm.degree' (2 to 5), 'svm.gamma' (4.5399929762484854e-05 to 22026.465794806718 with log-scale), and 'svm.tolerance' (4.5399929762484854e-05 to 2.0 with log-scale). Finally, if 'xgboost' is selected, the gradient boosting dynamics are governed by 'xgboost.booster' ('gblinear', 'gbtree', 'dart'), 'xgboost.nrounds' (7 to 2981 with log-scale), 'xgboost.eta' (0.0009118819655545162 to 1.0 with log-scale), 'xgboost.gamma' (4.5399929762484854e-05 to 7.38905609893065 with log-scale), 'xgboost.max_depth' (1 to 15), 'xgboost.min_child_weight' (2.718281828459045 to 148.4131591025766 with log-scale), 'xgboost.colsample_bytree' (0.01 to 1.0), 'xgboost.colsample_bylevel' (0.01 to 1.0), 'xgboost.lambda' (0.0009118819655545162 to 1096.6331584284585 with log-scale), 'xgboost.alpha' (0.0009118819655545162 to 1096.6331584284585 with log-scale), 'xgboost.subsample' (0.1 to 1.0), 'xgboost.rate_drop' (0.0 to 1.0), and 'xgboost.skip_drop' (0.0 to 1.0). Please note that while these specified ranges and categorical options define the absolute implementational boundaries and available choices for each parameter, they serve primarily as a reference frame; you can flexibly control the actual search space depending on your optimization strategy. The evaluation budget is {MAX_EVAL_VALUE}."
